  "category_grouping": "Label-free dataset definition: per categorical column, the 98 most frequent values over the source reports are kept and the rest become OTHER (state: 59). Fixed once when the dataset is built, before any benchmark split; no labels used.",
  "task_framing": "Retrospective classification of recorded report seriousness from restricted report contents. Not a forecast at vaccination time and not evidence about vaccine causation.",
  "population": "Domestic, non-manufacturer reports of reactions with onset 0-42 days after vaccination (or unknown onset); infection/breakthrough and vaccine-failure reports excluded; likely secondary reports of the same event collapsed. Restricted to reports for which the fixed extraction procedure retains a non-empty narrative excerpt (narrative_onset_policy). This disproportionately excludes serious reports (see counts.narrative_onset_empty_share_by_label and counts.cohort_filter); results apply to this selected cohort. Further restricted by the label-blind care-boundary-2 eligibility rules. Sampled by frequency matching (see sampling), so vaccine type, year, age band and sex carry little information about the label by design. Restricted to rows retaining an informative care-boundary-3 excerpt; prior matching ratios can change.",
  "narrative_onset_policy": "Literal prefix of v11a excerpt; additionally stop at named medication, clinical-care and procedure classes.",
  "sampling": "Frozen v11a matched IDs restricted by the label-blind care-boundary-3 text eligibility rule. No rematching.",
